---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Button from './Button.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/felipe-plets-portrait.jpg';

const facts = [
  { label: 'Writing code since', value: '1999' },
  { label: 'Leading teams since', value: '2006' },
  { label: 'Based in', value: 'Toronto' },
];
---

<Section id="about" eyebrow="About">
  <div class="grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[1.35fr_1fr] lg:gap-20">
    <div data-reveal>
      <h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">
        Two decades of shipping, spent on the same question.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          I started programming in 1999, tinkering with JavaScript because it was the
          fastest way to make something real appear on a screen. That instinct never left.
          Since then I have shipped production systems in Delphi, PHP, C#, Swift, Kotlin,
          Python, Ruby, ABAP, Java and &mdash; still &mdash; a great deal of JavaScript.
        </p>
        <p>
          I have been in leadership roles since 2006 &mdash; developer, Scrum Master, Agile
          Coach, Design Thinking Coach, team lead. Different titles, the same job: helping
          teams design a development lifecycle that produces consistent gains in
          productivity, quality, performance and security, and then actually holding the
          line on it. I grew up in that work in Brazil, and have been doing it in Toronto
          since immigrating to Canada.
        </p>
        <p>
          Today I work at Zensurance in Toronto and write about the shift happening around
          all of us. The promise of AI-assisted and agentic development is real, and so is
          the failure mode: organizations that get dramatically faster at producing code
          they no longer understand. My work is about taking the first outcome without the
          second.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10">
        <Button href="/about" variant="ghost" withArrow>More about my background</Button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="lg:pt-4" data-reveal>
      <figure class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-line">
        <Image
          src={portrait}
          alt="Felipe Plets"
          widths={[360, 560, 720]}
          sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 24rem, (min-width: 640px) 60vw, 90vw"
          class="h-auto w-full object-cover contrast-[1.02] saturate-[0.9]"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <div
          class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-ink via-ink/15 to-transparent"
        >
        </div>
        <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 mix-blend-soft-light bg-copper/25"></div>
      </figure>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-ink-soft/60 p-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p>
        <dl class="mt-6 space-y-6">
          {
            facts.map((fact) => (
              <div class="border-b border-line pb-5 last:border-0 last:pb-0">
                <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-faint">{fact.label}</dt>
                <dd class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl text-bone">{fact.value}</dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Section>
